    return `<details class="stakeholder-guide" open><summary>Who needs to be involved?</summary><div><p>Use this as a routing guide, then assess the actual incident, legal entity and contractual duties.</p><div class="stakeholder-cards"><article><b>Your team</b><p>Incident lead, security, operations, business owner and privacy / legal. Record times, impact, decisions and unknowns.</p></article><article><b>Customers and suppliers</b><p>Use agreed security contacts, escalation and evidence arrangements. A processor informs its controller without undue delay where Article 33(2) applies. ${sourceLink('gdpr','GDPR roles')}</p></article><article><b>Cyber assistance / notification</b><p>${esc(c.authority)} <a href="${esc(safeUrl(c.report))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official route ↗</a>. Confirm threshold, scope and current national procedure.</p></article><article><b>Personal-data breach</b><p>Assess controller notification and high-risk communication to individuals. <a href="${esc(safeUrl(c.privacy))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Competent DPA guidance ↗</a>.</p></article><article><b>Financial and product roles</b><p>Covered financial entities assess DORA and current competent-authority processes${c.financial?` · <a href="${esc(safeUrl(c.financial))}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${esc(c.financialLabel)} ↗</a>`:''}. Applicable manufacturers use the ${sourceLink('cra','CRA reporting process')}. Do not assume one report replaces every route.</p></article><article><b>AI issues and suspected crime</b><p>${sourceLink('aiNational','Find AI Act national resources and competent authorities')}. For suspected crime use the appropriate national police route; ${sourceLink('police','Europol lists national cybercrime routes')}.</p></article></div>${countrySelect()}<p class="source-note">Facts and assistance can be shared before the root cause is final. Use secure channels and minimise unnecessary personal data or secrets.</p></div></details>`;
